"""Hand-written mutants: domain-specific breakages a generic mutation tool cannot express.

Each entry is (group, name, target test file, patch code). The patch is executed in a
fresh interpreter before pytest imports the target, monkeypatching the module in place.
tests/mutation/test_mutants.py asserts every mutant is KILLED by its target file.

Removed relative to the old tools/mutate_*.py:
  G_z validate_finite_default_on  - the flag no longer exists.
  D_G forward_consumes_global_rng - the critic's forward has no RNG contract at module level
                                    (deleted with the PyTorch-verification tests); global-RNG
                                    reproducibility is covered by the trainer's bit-exact
                                    resume test once checkpoint.py exists.
"""

